      "description": "Nagasaki Shinchi Chinatown is the oldest Chinatown in Japan, dating back to the 17th century when Chinese traders settled near Dejima. Today its narrow streets are lined with vibrant restaurants, street food stalls serving champon and sara-udon, and colorful gates marking each cardinal direction.",
